<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-SOUTH AFRICA BEAT ZAMBIA IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SOUTH AFRICA BEAT ZAMBIA IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of a World Cup</p>
<p>African group three qualifier on Sunday:</p>
<p> South Africa   3   Zambia   0   (halftime 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Helman Mkhalele 9, Phil Masinga 16, Mark Williams 74.</p>
<p>Attendance: 70,000</p>
<p>    Standings		     P  W  D  L  F  A  Pts</p>
<p> South Africa		     5  3  1  1  6  3  10</p>
<p> Congo				4  2  1  1  4  4   7</p>
<p> Zambia			     5  1  2  2  5  6   5</p>
<p> Democratic Republic of Congo 4  0  2  2  4  6   2</p>
<p>Remaining matches: Congo v Democratic Republic of Congo</p>
<p>(formerly Zaire, in Pointe Noire), August 17 South Africa v</p>
<p>Congo (Johannesburg), Zambia v Democratic Republic of Congo</p>
<p>(Lusaka).</p>
